# The sound sets, one per line. scripts/pin.sh turns this into sets.txt (every
# file, with its address and SHA-256). Fields, separated by |:
#
#   id | name | role | licence | credit | GitHub repository | ref | the
#   instrument's .sfz in it | what to call it once installed | notice | patches
#
# ref is a commit (the sets stay as they were pinned until it is changed).
# One recommended instrument per set: the one .sfz named here is kept
# (renamed, nothing inside it is changed), with the files it plays and the
# licence and readme. patches, when not empty, is a glob (folder by folder,
# from the repository's root) of the set's other instruments, which the
# installers fetch only when asked for every patch. Every set is credited, whatever its licence. The
# notice is text a licence asks to be shown (empty when none).
#
# role is one of clean-guitars, overdriven-guitars, distorted-guitars,
# nylon-guitars, steel-guitars, basses, drums: the row of the MIDI plugin's settings
# window the set is offered for (mateusrdp/oxiguitar#152). The MIDI plugin plays,
# where nothing is picked, the set whose role names the row: two sets for a row
# would leave the choice to chance, so a set that is installed to be picked and
# never played by itself has the role none.
